# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("`rebuild`": a generation is built at the end of the tick its dynamic changes, the old one leaves at the end of that tick) and the dynamic law as ruled for structural dynamics (round 3 ST): the `rebuild`'s dynamic is published at the first firing of the tick after the generation is built, where `!Updated` of it fires once; never run.
test the_block_hears_the_rebuild_below

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")
    2: Ui.Label(text="2 heard 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    1/#1/0: Ui.Label(text="page 2")
  torn down:
    1/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")

tick 2
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="4 heard 1")

test a_row_hears_the_rebuild_below

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x heard 0")
    2/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    2/#1/0: Ui.Label(text="page 2")
  torn down:
    2/#0/0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")

tick 2
  changed:
    1/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x heard 1")
